<article class="env-theorem" id="0DIQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DIQ">Theorem <span data-tag="0DIQ">77.13.6</span> <span class="named">(Derived Grothendieck Existence Theorem)</span>.</a>  In Situation <a href="/tag/0DIK" data-tag="0DIK">77.13.1</a> there exists a pseudo-coherent $K$ in $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ such that $K_ n = K \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X}^\mathbf {L} \mathcal{O}_{X_ n}$ for all $n$ compatibly with the maps $\varphi _ n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Lemmas <a href="/tag/0DIL" data-tag="0DIL">77.13.2</a>, <a href="/tag/0DIM" data-tag="0DIM">77.13.3</a>, <a href="/tag/0DIN" data-tag="0DIN">77.13.4</a> to get a pseudo-coherent object $K$ of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. Choosing affine $U$ in Lemma <a href="/tag/0DIP" data-tag="0DIP">77.13.5</a> it follows immediately that $K$ restricts to $K_ n$ over $X_ n$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>